    "content": "{\"id\": \"19900cf9-0298-4b65-ad3f-630fd49aad38\", \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"**I couldn't find any model package approval status, because nothing in this account and region is registered in the SageMaker Model Registry.** I checked account 123456789012 in us-east-1.\\n\\n**What I found**\\n- There are no model package groups and no model packages, so there are no versions and no approval statuses.\\n- Four endpoints are InService: `my-llm-ep`, `opsai-fx-async-ep`, `opsai-fx-serverless-ep` and `opsai-fx-idle-ep`.\\n- `my-llm-ep` serves the model `opsai-fx-model-faulty`. It was created directly from a model artifact in S3 (`s3://opsai-fx-sm-c8e0a7c3/model/model.tar.gz`) with a stock scikit-learn container. It has no link to a registry package. Its environment variables also include `FAIL_RATE=0.3`, which looks like a test setting.\\n- The only other model, `hf-llm-falcon-7b-instruct-bf16-\\u2026`, is a JumpStart Falcon 7B deployment. It also has no registry link.\\n- I didn't look at the other three endpoints' configs. Their names suggest they use `opsai-fx-model`, which is also unregistered.\\n\\nSo the version you're serving didn't come through a Model Registry approval. If a fine-tuned model was meant to be gated by approval, the deployment is bypassing that gate.\\n\\n**What I haven't checked**\\n- Other regions. The registry may live in a different region than us-east-1.\\n- Other accounts. A shared or central registry could be in another account, and this agent space may not be associated with it.\\n\\nIf you tell me the region or account, or the name of the model package group you expected, I can check there. I can also check the other three endpoints' configs.\", \"type\": \"text\"}], \"created_at\": null}",
